# JSONPath Exam Challenges: Solutions & Breakdown

> [!TIP]
> Permitted Exam Reference: [JSONPath Support](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/kubectl/jsonpath/) | [kubectl Cheat Sheet - Formatting Output](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/kubectl/cheatsheet/#formatting-output)

## Solution 1: Node Internal IPs

```bash
kubectl get nodes -o jsonpath='{.items[*].status.addresses[?(@.type=="InternalIP")].address}'
```

## Solution 2: Node Architecture and OS Images

```bash
kubectl get nodes -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{"\t"}{.status.nodeInfo.architecture}{"\t"}{.status.nodeInfo.osImage}{"\n"}{end}'
```

Alternative via custom-columns:

```bash
kubectl get nodes -o custom-columns=NAME:.metadata.name,ARCH:.status.nodeInfo.architecture,OS:.status.nodeInfo.osImage
```

## Solution 3: kube-system Pod Names

```bash
kubectl get pods -n kube-system -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{"\n"}{end}'
```

## Solution 4: Control Plane Component Images

```bash
kubectl get pods -n kube-system -l component=kube-apiserver -o jsonpath='{.items[0].spec.containers[0].image}'
```

## Solution 5: Pods Sorted by Creation Timestamp

```bash
kubectl get pods -n kube-system --sort-by='.metadata.creationTimestamp'
```

## Solution 6: Service Names and ClusterIPs

```bash
kubectl get svc -A -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{"\t"}{.spec.clusterIP}{"\n"}{end}'
```

## Solution 7: Find Non-Running Pods

```bash
kubectl get pods -A -o jsonpath='{.items[?(@.status.phase!="Running")].metadata.name}'
```

## Solution 8: ConfigMap Keys

```bash
kubectl get configmap kube-root-ca.crt -n default -o jsonpath='{.data}'
```

## Solution 9: PersistentVolume Capacities

```bash
kubectl get pv -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{"\t"}{.spec.capacity.storage}{"\n"}{end}'
```

## Solution 10: Node Capacity CPU and Memory

```bash
kubectl get nodes -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}{"\t"}{.status.capacity.cpu}{"\t"}{.status.allocatable.memory}{"\n"}{end}'
```
